# Whether an interval with one-limb bounds is the whole line (milestone2.md, "One enclosure
# interface", the row of is_entire()): x_l = -inf and x_u = +inf. Exact; false for the empty set
# (+inf, -inf). For every precision.
kernel:        interval_entire_1
input:         stored xl
input:         stored xu
output:        mask m
requires:      interval xl xu
ensures:       certain m entire x x=xl,xu exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the two bounds compared with the infinities (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand

mi = neg(const inf)
a  = eq(xl, mi)
b  = eq(xu, const inf)
m  = and(a, b)
